ps: &B) -> usize;\n    fn group_matches(&self, groups: &B, index: usize, id: &Id) -> bool;\n    fn member_length(&self, groups: &B, group: usize) -> usize;\n    fn member_matches(&self, groups: &B, group: usize, index: usize, note: &Id) -> bool;\n    fn trigger_length(&self, groups: &B, group: usize) -> usize;\n    fn trigger_matches(&self, groups: &B, group: usize, index: usize, note: &Id) -> bool;\n\n    fn prepend_member(&self, groups: B, group: usize, note: &Id) -> B;\n    fn prepend_trigger(&self, groups: B, group: usize, note: &Id) -> B;\n    fn remove_trigger(&self, groups: B, group: usize, index: usize) -> B;\n    fn append_empty(&self, groups: B, id: &Id) -> B;\n    fn swap_groups(&self, groups: B, left: usize, right: usize) -> B;\n}","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Point laws required by the extracted proof:"},{"DocComment":" - source reads preserve the full immutable source, including duplicate notes;"},{"DocComment":" - matches compares exact IDs, without converting them to machine indices;"},{"DocComment":" - prepend_* inserts at zero and changes only that one group's named list;"},{"DocComment":" - remove_trigger removes exactly the specified slot (not all equal IDs);"},{"DocComment":" - append_empty appends one group with the supplied ID and two empty lists;"},{"DocComment":" - swap_groups exchanges exactly two outer-list slots, preserving both groups;"},{"DocComment":" - every other group/field and all unaffected lengths are unchanged."},{"DocComment":" Indexed reads/mutations require in-bounds indices; insert/append also need"},{"DocComment":" successful allocation and representable resulting lengths."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":true,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"S"},{"index":2,"name":"B"},{"index":3,"name":"Id"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},